PROJECT_MANAGEMENT_STANDARD_VERSION 0.1.0

STATUS DRAFT

OWNER President Cley Duarte

SCOPE ORGANIZATION

DEPENDS_ON

protocols/LEARNING_PROTOCOL_0.1.0.pdl (this standard was promoted from a
  REQUEST through that protocol)

PURPOSE

Fix the external, day-to-day management shape every PACE-governed project
takes in the tracking tool, so a new project is set up the same way every
time, in seconds, without re-deciding structure. PACE's .pace/ memory
stays tool-agnostic; this standard lives one level out, at the
organization, describing how the work is TRACKED — not what the knowledge
IS.

TOOL

ClickUp, at workspace level. Each governed unit is a FOLDER inside the
organization's Space; the project's work lives in ONE list inside its own
folder.

FOLDER_PER_PROJECT

Every governed project gets its own ClickUp FOLDER named after the
project, a sibling of the other projects' folders — never a set of loose
lists scattered inside another project's folder.

SINGLE_ORDERED_LIST

Each governed project has exactly ONE task list, ordered by a PHASE
methodology with a single continuous correlative — not a spread of lists
split by state.

  - Every task is named  "FN . NN . Title"  where FN is its phase (F1, F2,
    ...) and NN is a global correlative that never repeats and never
    resets across phases (01, 02, 03 ...).
  - Phases group the work in time; the correlative keeps strict order and
    prevents drift. A phase label is valid only if every earlier phase
    also exists (no "F3" without a real F1 and F2).
  - Completed items come first; task STATE is carried by the status column
    (to do / in progress / complete), never by a separate list.
  - A final "someday/maybe" phase (highest FN) at the lowest priority
    holds future ideas in the same list.

Rationale: for a single owner focused on execution, five lists split by
state add places to look without adding clarity. One ordered, phased list
reads top-to-bottom and stays honest. (Supersedes the five-list layout.
Promoted from REQUEST-0010 and refined with the phase-plus-correlative
nomenclature the ROOT_AUTHORITY chose.)

SEEDING

On project setup, the ordered list is populated from the project's own
roadmap in .pace/, one task per step, each marked DONE or PENDING against
the real state of the repository — never an empty board.

CORRESPONDENCE

ClickUp is the volatile, human-facing operational view; .pace/ is the
durable, AI-facing memory. A task outcome that carries lasting meaning (a
decision, a shipped release, a lesson) is recorded back into .pace/ as
the appropriate entity — the board is disposable, the memory is not.

ORIGIN

Promoted from REQUEST-0002 (ClickUp way of working as PACE structure).
Refined by REQUEST-0010: one ordered list instead of five, state by
status, and a single phase-plus-correlative numbering (FN . NN).

END
